<title>SPAIN: Spain's Argentaria launches new fund.</title>
<headline>Spain's Argentaria launches new fund.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Argentaria said on Wednesday it had launched a new fund for institutional investors.</p>
<p>The fund offers guaranteed short-term returns with immediate liquidity and no refund commission. The minimum investment is for 750 million pesetas, the bank said.</p>
<p>The minimum return will be linked to MIBOR rates and 15 and 30 day repo rates. The first one-month and three-month guaranteed returns will be 5.6 percent and 5.08 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The bank's management commission will be 0.10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
